"""Dataset augmentation for the intent classifier.

WHY
---
The handwritten set in `intent_dataset.py` is 344 examples across 28 classes
(~12 each).  Every classifier family tested — logistic regression, linear
SVM, complement naive Bayes, random forest, and an MLP — plateaued at
77-79% 5-fold accuracy.  When six unrelated architectures agree, the limit
is the data, not the model.

Voice commands are genuinely templated ("open X", "close X", "play X"), so
slot expansion produces realistic rather than synthetic-looking data.  For
the open-ended classes (conversation, coding_assistant) templates would
produce unnatural text, so those stay handwritten and are extended by hand.

Prefix/suffix noise ("umm", "please", "for me") is applied to a sampled
subset because real STT output carries exactly that kind of filler.
"""

